When an aggregate sends all its changes to another application, it must have a version
property. The application that receives the changes uses this version property to apply all
changes in the right order. An explicit version number is necessary because changes are
sent asynchronously, so the order they are received may differ from the order they were
sent. For this purpose, events that are used to publish changes outside of the application
have both OldVersion (the version before the change) and NewVersion (the version after
the change) properties. Events associated with delete events have no NewVersion, since
after being deleted, an entity can't store any versions.
